        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0418" n="306" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 1199/176–177.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister McCreery to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic">May 18,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a copy and
                    translation of act of the National Congress, signed by the President on the 14th
                    instant, declaring a loan of $20,000,000 for the amortization of the debt of the
                    Republic and the redemption of certain concessions to be for public good.</p>
                <p>This is done under paragraph 11 of article 25 of the constitution, defining as an
                    attribute of the Congress: “To decree the making of loans on the credit of the
                    nation. No loan shall be voted without a previous decree that it is for the
                    public good.”</p>
                <p>Contracts made by the Dominican Government for the loan above referred to will be
                    discussed by the Congress next week. It is said that a number of changes and
                    amendments will be proposed and a considerable discussion is expected.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fenton R.
                    McCreery.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d262-a1.xml" xpointer="d262-a1"/>
            </div>
